==Known Issues - Aiming to be Fixed at a Later Date==
===Last Updated: Monday, December 2nd, 4:40pm===
Since the status of these issues isn't going to change, we'll use a list here to keep things a little more concise!

===Clue-related Issues===
* The Clue Compass teleport for "Search Upstairs in the houses of Seers' Village for some drawers" isn't working as intended.
* The Clue Compass teleport for Miscellania requires quest completion even though you can access Miscellania without finishing the quest.
* The Clue Compass teleport for the Drunken Dwarf in Keldagrim requires completion of The Giant Dwarf.
* Some S.T.A.S.H. Units from Varlamore: The Rising Darkness are missing from the Clue Compass.
* Using the Clue Compass to teleport to your current step doesn't work if your last teleport was to the same step.

===Relic-or Mastery-related Issues===
* Herbiboar doesn't interact correctly with Friendly Forager.
* Mining Gloves aren't correctly increasing the number of successful Mining rolls you can perform if used in conjunction with the Echo pickaxe.

===Miscellaneous Issues===
* Lovakite Ore depleted after one successful Mining roll, rather than the intended 4 when using the Echo pickaxe.
* Players reported that buying Mind Rune packs with a full Inventory still took their GP. Aubury will be accosted accordingly.
* Players report that obtaining the Quetzin didn't complete the task for obtaining a Skilling pet.
* The 'Relic Icon' setting to make your relics visible above your message box will re-enable itself on every login, which can be frustrating.
* The Medium Lumbridge Achievement Diary task to "Craft a coif in the Lumbridge Cow Pen" cannot be completed if the player inlocks Tirannwn, Varlamore, Wilderness and Overgrown or Pocket Kingdom.
* Canifis is spelled incorrectly on the Clue Compass teleport menu, making the game literally unplayable.

That's all we've got for now, but we'll be coming back to this post at the end of the day for an update, and continuing to update this post between now and next week's Game Update.

We hope you're having fun in Leagues V: Raging Echoes, we know we are!

